<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Venice Protocol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> Protocol was an agreement signed on 13 October 1921 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> under Italian mediation to settle the dispute over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a>. Hungary undertook to withdraw its irregular forces from the region and hand it over to Austria, while a plebiscite was to decide the future of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sopron">Sopron</a> and its surroundings. The vote, held in December 1921, kept Sopron in Hungary.</p></div>
